Carafe: DXVK-Sarek's choices for the frame rate limiter. dxvk.frameRateMethod (or DXVK_FRAME_RATE_METHOD) is
"timeline", DXVK's own cadence and the default, "deviation", the limiter of DXVK 1.x that carries the error of one
frame into the next, or "reactive", which waits a whole frame from every present. dxvk.frameRatePacing (or
DXVK_FRAME_RATE_PACING) is how the wait is spent: "precise", DXVK's sleep with a busy wait for its last
milliseconds and the default, "sleep", one sleep and no busy wait, "sliced", sleeps of at most 1 ms with a busy
wait for the last 0.15 ms, or "spin", a busy wait throughout.
Zlib, as the files it changes.

